'''Hermione "Harmony" Bagwa'''<ref name="CVD, NE">''[[Star Wars: The Complete Visual Dictionary, New Edition]]''</ref> was a [[Gender|female]] [[human]] who worked as a [[Waiter|waitress]] alongside [[Wanda (human)|Wanda]] and [[FLO]] at [[Dex's Diner]], an [[Restaurant|eatery]] owned by [[Dexter Jettster]] and located on the streets of [[CoCo Town]], [[Coruscant]].<ref name="sweDD">{{SWE|locations|dexsdiner|Dex's Diner}}</ref> She grew up within Coruscant's [[Coruscant Underworld|underworld]].<ref name="CVD, NE" /> Shortly before the onset of the [[Clone Wars]], Bagwa was present in the diner when [[Jedi Knight]] [[Obi-Wan Kenobi]] visited Jettster regarding a mysterious [[Kamino saberdart|saberdart]].<ref name="AOC" />

{{Char-stub}}

==Behind the scenes==
Hermione Bagwa was portrayed by Australian actress [[Susie Porter]] in the [[2002]] film [[Star Wars: Episode II Attack of the Clones|''Star Wars'': Episode II ''Attack of the Clones'']], the second installment of the ''[[Star Wars]]'' [[prequel trilogy]].<ref name="AOC" /> 

Early production notes for ''Attack of the Clones'' suggest that Bagwa was originally going to be Dexter Jettster's wife instead of his waitress, but this direction was ultimately abandoned. During filming, Porter delivered waitress lines as both Hermione and [[FLO]], the latter who was the only one to have a speaking part in the finished film.<ref name="DB">{{DB|character|hermionebagwa|Bagwa, Hermione}}</ref>

